              "body": "**Late binding is a feature at least as often as it is a bug.** It is what makes `nonlocal` counters, memoization caches, and mutable closure state work at all, and what lets a decorator read a configuration variable that is set after the decorator is applied. The rule to apply is not 'avoid closures in loops' but: *if the closure should see the value as-of creation, make it a default argument or a factory parameter; if it should see the value as-of call, capture it freely.* State which you meant."
