              "body": "**A `__getattr__` that does not raise `AttributeError` for genuinely missing names will break the standard library.** `copy`, `pickle`, `inspect`, and `unittest.mock` all probe for optional attributes (`__deepcopy__`, `__getstate__`, `__wrapped__`) and rely on `AttributeError` meaning 'not present'. A `__getattr__` that returns a default for *every* name makes those probes succeed and hands the library a nonsense object; one that raises `KeyError` makes them explode. Always end with `raise AttributeError(name)`."
