                  "prompt": "A class uses `@property` to validate `temperature` on assignment. A colleague, wanting to skip validation in a hot loading path, writes `obj.__dict__['temperature'] = raw`. Explain what the class then reports for `obj.temperature`, whether the invariant is preserved, and what this says about where invariants can be enforced.",
