              "body": "**Descriptors only work on classes, not on instances.** Assigning a descriptor to an instance attribute (`obj.attr = Positive()`) stores an ordinary object: the protocol is invoked only for descriptors found on the *type* (step 1 of the lookup algorithm), so `obj.attr` returns the descriptor object itself and `__get__` is never called. This is the same type-versus-instance rule as special methods in Unit 3, and it has the same fix: put it on the class."
