              "type": "theorem",
              "kind": "theorem",
              "name": "Retry safety requires idempotence",
              "statement": "Let an operation O be retried after a failure whose cause does not distinguish *'O never executed'* from *'O executed but the acknowledgement was lost'*. Then retrying is safe — produces the same final state as a single successful execution — if and only if O is **idempotent**: executing O twice leaves the same state as executing it once.\n\nCorollary: a read timeout is not safely retryable for a non-idempotent operation, while a connect timeout is, because the latter *does* distinguish the cases.",
